UGLY: Ultimate Glue LaYer
=========================

UGLY is a C library for in-process calls between programming languages. It
embeds the real interpreters and VMs and routes every cross-language call
through a small, language-neutral C core. Each language needs one plugin (so
the core can call into it) and one binding (so it can call the core), which
makes 2N adapters instead of N^2 pairwise bridges.

It is an unfinished prototype from 2013-2014. The Perl 5 plugin works end to
end and is frozen as the v1 reference. The early Java plugin was removed and
survives in the v0.01 tag. The next plugins planned are Lua, CPython and
QuickJS.

See README.md for the architecture, current status and build instructions, and
doc/design-essay.md for the design discussion.
